       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is about 5 times the usual maximum for an adult (3,200 mg/day, or 1,200 mg/day for OTC use). A single 4,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At that level the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg really is what you intend, tell me that and the clinical rationale, and I'll go from there."
