       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily (16,000 mg/day) has no recognized therapeutic use. It is in the range associated with serious toxicity, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, CNS depression, and severe metabolic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nYou can still get the patient what they need:\n- **If the dose was a slip,** give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. Common regimens are 400 mg PO QID, 600 mg PO QID, or 800 mg PO TID.\n- **If there's an unusual clinical reason,** talk to your attending and the clinical pharmacist first. The order would need their review and sign-off, and most systems would require a documented override.\n- **If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect,** I can help you put together a safer multimodal regimen, for example scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nWhat would you like to do?"
      }
